    <item>
      <title>Foundational Mechanics, Sensing, and Complex Dynamical Systems</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/research-themes/foundational-mechanics/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/research-themes/foundational-mechanics/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This thrust focuses on foundational mechanics, computational representations, sensing concepts, and complex dynamical systems that support structural health monitoring, digital twins, and resilient infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The aim is to develop mathematical, mechanical, and computational tools that help represent structural behaviour in ways that are physically meaningful, interpretable, and useful for monitoring, prognosis, and decision support. This thrust also provides space for exploratory work inspired by bio-inspired sensing and active-matter-like collective dynamics where such ideas can inform sensing, modelling, or infrastructure monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Activities</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/activities/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/activities/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This page highlights selected academic activities, invited lectures, workshops, outreach efforts, and professional engagements connected to teaching, research, and the development of RISE Lab.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Workshops and Short Courses&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;workshops-and-short-courses&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#workshops-and-short-courses&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;activity-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;activity-card featured-activity&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;activity-badge workshop-badge&#34;&gt;Upcoming Workshop&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Machine Learning for Scientific Computing&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;activity-meta&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Role:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinator &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Venue:&lt;/strong&gt; Indian Institute of Technology Bombay &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Date:&lt;/strong&gt; July 23–24, 2026 &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Status:&lt;/strong&gt; Upcoming&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xD;&#xA;This workshop introduces machine learning methods for scientific computing and engineering applications, with emphasis on traditional numerical methods, physics-informed learning, surrogate modelling, and data-driven solution of differential equations.&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Join</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/join/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/join/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;RISE Lab is actively looking for motivated &lt;strong&gt;PhD students&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;M.Tech students&lt;/strong&gt;, and highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;B.Tech students&lt;/strong&gt; interested in smart and resilient infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The group works at the interface of structural engineering, sensing, computer vision, AI/ML, scientific computing, digital twins, structural health monitoring, prognosis, and infrastructure resilience.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Specific project topics are discussed individually after understanding the student’s background, interests, expected time commitment, and available research opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;PhD Students&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;phd-students&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#phd-students&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am especially interested in recruiting PhD students who want to work on long-term research problems related to smart infrastructure, structural health monitoring, physics-guided sensing, computer vision, AI/ML, digital twins, scientific machine learning, uncertainty-aware prognosis, and resilient infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Uncertainty-Aware SHM and Bayesian Inference</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/research-themes/uncertainty-aware-shm/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/research-themes/uncertainty-aware-shm/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This thrust focuses on uncertainty-aware methods for structural health monitoring, damage diagnosis, model updating, prognosis, and decision support.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The goal is to move from deterministic monitoring outputs toward confidence-aware interpretation, where engineers can understand not only what a model predicts, but also how reliable that prediction may be.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;What We Study&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;what-we-study&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#what-we-study&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-project-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-project-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Uncertainty-Aware Monitoring&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Methods for understanding how measurement noise, modelling assumptions, environmental variability, and limited data affect infrastructure monitoring outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Team</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/team/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/team/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RISE Lab — Resilient Infrastructure and Smart Engineering Lab&lt;/strong&gt; is a growing research group in the Department of Civil Engineering at IIT Bombay.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The group works on smart and resilient infrastructure systems through structural health monitoring, physics-guided sensing, computer vision, AI/ML, digital twins, prognosis, and decision support.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Faculty Lead&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;faculty-lead&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#faculty-lead&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;team-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;team-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/images/team/ashish-pal.jpeg&#34; class=&#34;team-photo&#34; alt=&#34;Prof. Ashish Pal&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Prof. Ashish Pal&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;prof-ashish-pal&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#prof-ashish-pal&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;team-role&#34;&gt;Assistant Professor&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Department of Civil Engineering&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Indian Institute of Technology Bombay&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Scientific Machine Learning and Equation Discovery</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/research-themes/scientific-machine-learning/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/research-themes/scientific-machine-learning/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This thrust focuses on scientific machine learning methods for understanding structural and dynamical systems from data.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The emphasis is on combining data-driven learning with mechanics, governing principles, physical constraints, and computational models so that machine learning methods remain meaningful for engineering analysis and infrastructure monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;What We Study&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;what-we-study&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#what-we-study&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-project-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-project-card&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Scientific Machine Learning for Engineering Systems&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Methods that combine machine learning with physical principles, numerical modelling, and engineering knowledge for structural and infrastructure applications.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Teaching</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/teaching/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/teaching/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;My teaching focuses on building strong foundations in structural engineering, mechanics, numerical methods, and computational thinking. I aim to connect classical civil engineering concepts with modern computational tools, simulations, and research-oriented problem solving.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Courses Taught&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;courses-taught&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#courses-taught&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;research-card&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Reinforced Concrete Design&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;reinforced-concrete-design&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#reinforced-concrete-design&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Undergraduate course covering the fundamentals of reinforced concrete behaviour and design, including flexure, shear, serviceability, limit state design philosophy, and practical design considerations for structural members.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Projects</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/projects/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/projects/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Research projects at &lt;strong&gt;RISE Lab&lt;/strong&gt; focus on smart and resilient infrastructure systems through sensing, structural health monitoring, computer vision, AI/ML, digital twins, prognosis, and decision support.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The projects listed here represent ongoing sponsored, internal, exploratory, and collaborative research activities.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Sponsored Research Projects&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;sponsored-research-projects&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#sponsored-research-projects&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-grid&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-card featured-project&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;project-badge&#34;&gt;ANRF Early Career Research Grant&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;High-Fidelity Digital Twins via Scientific Discovery Using Physics-Informed Machine Learning and Uncertainty Quantification for Structural Health Monitoring and Performance Assessment&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;project-meta&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Funding Agency:&lt;/strong&gt; Anusandhan National Research Foundation (ANRF) &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Scheme:&lt;/strong&gt; Early Career Research Grant &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Role:&lt;/strong&gt; Principal Investigator &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Status:&lt;/strong&gt; Ongoing &lt;br&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; Three years&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Research Publications</title>
      <link>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/publications/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/publications/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The publications below reflect research in structural health monitoring, nonlinear system identification, scientific machine learning, sensor fusion, uncertainty quantification, digital twins, and smart and resilient infrastructure systems.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Prospective PhD and M.Tech students are encouraged to explore these papers to understand the group’s research style, technical foundations, and broader areas of interest.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://10.52.0.204:1313/ashish-pal-website/join/&#34; &gt;View research opportunities →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;style&gt;&#xD;&#xA;.publication-section {&#xD;&#xA;  margin-top: 3rem;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.publication-section h2 {&#xD;&#xA;  color: #0f172a;&#xD;&#xA;  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;&#xD;&#xA;  font-size: 1.45rem;&#xD;&#xA;  font-weight: 800;&#xD;&#xA;  line-height: 1.25;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.dark .publication-section h2 {&#xD;&#xA;  color: white;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.publication-list {&#xD;&#xA;  display: grid;&#xD;&#xA;  gap: 1.15rem;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.publication-card {&#xD;&#xA;  padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;&#xD;&#xA;  border-radius: 18px;&#xD;&#xA;  background: #ffffff;&#xD;&#xA;  border: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);&#xD;&#xA;  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);&#xD;&#xA;  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);&#xD;&#xA;  transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.dark .publication-card {&#xD;&#xA;  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);&#xD;&#xA;  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);&#xD;&#xA;  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.18);&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.publication-card:hover {&#xD;&#xA;  transform: translateY(-3px);&#xD;&#xA;  box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.dark .publication-card:hover {&#xD;&#xA;  box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.25);&#xD;&#xA;}&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;.pub